  "id": "lightdark-cycle",
  "term": "light–dark cycle",
  "definition": "The light–dark cycle is the regular daily alternation of light and darkness used to match animals’ natural day–night rhythm. In this context, it signals resting versus active periods, with darkness marking the phase when rats are typically more active.",
